+## Optional GF admission overlay (gf-admission 0.1.0rc2)
+
+The exact g5 overlay adds connection hello/close hooks and a dispatcher shutdown
+resource guard. `GF_ADMISSION_CONFIG` is default off and immutable per process.
+Enabled workers use the existing `fgjsq_v1` message envelope with versioned
+`admission_*` operations; ordinary server dispatch still has the 5s timeout.
+A single worker long poll is also the liveness heartbeat, even during inference
+and idle periods. Mgmt owns one broker under the original FG reservation lock.
+Queue residence carries neither P nor D reservations. READY has a claim lease;
+CLAIMED is not released merely because a heartbeat disappears. Drain/reconcile
+workers before destroying workload SHM; unresolved ownership refuses teardown.
+Implementation/tests and install contract are maintained in the parent
+llm-slo-scheduler repository, not in native engine scheduling.
+
+The optional admission protocol is schema2 (FG events remain schema1). Motor only
+increments attempt_seq AFTER allocation succeeds. Confirmed UNAVAILABLE therefore
+permits a new admission submission_round for the same attempt; lost acknowledgments
+must retain the original round. Expired worker ownership allows query/cancel/finish,
+not new claims or allocations. A dead owner's CLAIMED ticket can close only with
+explicit same-record native/FG release evidence, never merely lease expiry.
+Provider preparation bounds include candidate RPC and executor; a timed-out thread
+retains its permit until completion. Bounded residual samples filter before limiting.
