+# [2026-10-22] GF admission retries, expired owners and preparation bounds
+
+- Symptom: unavailable P could permanently pin one Motor attempt; expired owner could not finish a released ticket; metadata RPC bypassed feature deadline/capacity; residual sample hid later live claims.
+- Root cause: Motor increments attempt_seq only after allocation, but admission treated attempt as a single submission; liveness checks were reused for cleanup; feature accounting began after metadata; snapshot truncated before filtering.
+- Why: unit success paths missed outer router retries, control-plane outages and late residual records.
+- Fix: schema2 submission rounds only after confirmed UNAVAILABLE without reservation; immutable transport retry identity; expired-owner cleanup without lease revival plus per-record proven-release reconciliation; end-to-end preparation permit/deadline; residual-first pagination.
+- Test interception: parent tests test_motor_retry_same_attempt_recovers_in_off_and_enforce; test_confirmed_unavailable_resubmits_without_reclassification; test_expired_owner_cleanup_without_reviving_lease; test_metadata_rpc_obeys_total_feature_deadline_and_capacity; test_residual_sample_filters_before_limit_and_reports_truncation. These ran through Motor tests/run_tests.sh. Preserve uncertain CAS and live CLAIMED records.
+- Scenario: unavailable-to-ready P, lost heartbeat during inference, slow metadata and many terminal records ahead of a live claim.
+- Keywords: admission, submission_round, expired owner, deadline, residual.
